CLINICAL USE - READ THIS BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE
==============================================

THIS SOFTWARE IS NOT A MEDICAL DEVICE AND MUST NOT BE USED TO MAKE, INFORM, OR
DELAY ANY CLINICAL DECISION.

It is an unfinished student project. Specifically, and verifiably from this
repository's own documentation:

  * NO CLINICIAN HAS EVER REVIEWED ITS OUTPUT. Exit Gate 3 of the build plan
    requires agreement with a clinician on a gold-standard case set. That review
    has not happened. There is no measured agreement rate, no sensitivity, no
    specificity, and no error rate. Anyone quoting an accuracy figure for this
    system is quoting a number that does not exist.

  * EVERY CLINICAL THRESHOLD IN THE DATABASE IS A DEVELOPMENT PLACEHOLDER. They
    are marked as such in the data itself
    (source = 'DEVELOPMENT PLACEHOLDER - NOT A CLINICAL SOURCE'). They are
    plausible values chosen for development. They are not any hospital's critical
    value list, and they are not derived from any published standard.

  * THE KNOWLEDGE BASE SHIPS ONE FABRICATED DEMONSTRATION DOCUMENT, labelled as
    fabricated in its title, its source reference, and its publisher field. No
    WHO, ICMR, antibiogram, or national formulary content is loaded.

  * NO NOTIFICATION CAN LEAVE THE BUILDING. The SMS and email adapters are
    written but never registered. Every escalation rung silently degrades to an
    in-app message. The final rung - contacting the patient directly - CANNOT
    REACH A PATIENT.

  * IT HAS NOT BEEN REGULATORY-ASSESSED under CDSCO (India), FDA (United States),
    the EU MDR, or any other medical device framework, and no such assessment has
    been sought.

Using this software in patient care could cause a real result to be missed, a
real escalation to be trusted when it cannot be delivered, or a real clinical
threshold to be applied that no laboratory ever approved.


