WHAT THIS LICENSE CAN AND CANNOT DO - STATED HONESTLY
======================================================

The authors would rather write this down than let anyone rely on a protection
that does not exist. This project's whole discipline is refusing to claim more
than is true, and a licence is not an exception.

  * WHAT IT COVERS. Copyright protects this SOURCE CODE and the EXPRESSION in it -
    the files, the schema definitions, the rule implementations, the interface
    code, the documentation, and the diagrams. Copying, porting, or closely
    paraphrasing any of that without permission is an infringement, and that is
    enforceable.

  * WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER. Copyright does not protect an IDEA. Somebody who
    reads this README, never opens the source, and independently builds their own
    system that blocks a discharge until a test has an owner is not infringing
    this licence. Only a granted patent would reach that, and no patent has been
    filed or granted for this work.

  * THEREFORE, IF THE IDEA MATTERS COMMERCIALLY, the protection is not this file.
    It is shipping first, holding the clinical validation, holding the hospital
    relationships, and - if it is worth the cost - seeking formal IP advice.
    Publishing a public repository is itself a disclosure, and in most
    jurisdictions public disclosure starts a clock on what can still be patented.

  * THIS FILE IS NOT LEGAL ADVICE, and its authors are not lawyers. It states the
    copyright holder's terms clearly and in good faith. Before relying on it in a
    commercial dispute, or before a hospital deployment, get it reviewed by a
    qualified professional.
